course: dictionary
lesson: 2523
title: Decoding words and messages
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To decode something is to work out its meaning when it is hidden or written in a code. You change it back into words you can understand. Readers decode too: they turn letters into sounds and blend the sounds together to say a word.
explain: «Accurate decoding means reading every sound in order; guessing means saying a word that just looks similar.» Decoding is careful, step-by-step reading. Try it with a made-up word such as «zib». You cannot remember it, so you must sound it out, z-i-b, and blend the sounds into one word.
explain: Codes work the same way. In the code where IFMMP means HELLO, every letter is shifted one step forward in the alphabet. To decode, move each letter one step back: I becomes H, F becomes E, and so on. Check your answer by asking whether it makes sense.
fact: To decode means to change a message back into normal words so you can understand it.
fact: In reading, decoding means turning letters into sounds and blending them to say a word.
fact: Accurate decoding reads every sound in order; guessing only says a word that looks similar.
fact: Made-up words such as «zib» show whether a reader is decoding the sounds or guessing from memory.
fact: Decoding can also mean understanding a hidden meaning, like a strange look or difficult instructions.
exercise: In reading, what does it mean to decode a word? | Guess it from the picture | Write it in capital letters | *Turn its letters into sounds and blend them | Skip it and read on
exercise: In the code where IFMMP means HELLO, how do you decode a letter? | Swap it for a picture | Move it one step forward | *Move it one step back in the alphabet | Turn it into a number only
exercise: Why is «zib» a useful test word? | It is the longest word in the book | It rhymes with every other word | Its meaning is easy to remember | *It shows whether a child is decoding the sounds or guessing
test: «Accurate decoding means reading every sound in order; guessing means saying a word that just looks similar.» Which one is guessing? | *Saying a word that just looks similar | Reading each sound in order | Blending the letters c-a-t | Checking the sounds again
test: A message reads KHOOR, and each letter was shifted one step forward. What is the decoded word? | *JGNNQ | IFMMP | HELLO | LIPPS
exam: What does it mean to decode a hidden meaning? | Ignore it and move on | Read it aloud as fast as you can | *Work out what it really means | Write it down in a secret code
